 "limits": "Population: public GitHub, 2024-10-07..10 UTC (four weekdays of one autumn week). Developers on GitHub are skewed towards professional, English-speaking and North-American/European/Asian time zones; private repositories and private activity are invisible. GH Archive records the public events API, which drops events under load and omits some activity; counts are lower bounds. Stars are cheap signals inflated by automation and star farming; a star is not evidence of useful adoption (MASTER_SPEC 6.5). These models describe engagement dynamics, not usefulness. Observational associations only: nothing was randomized, so the models do not say what promotion, ranking or buying stars would cause. Short horizon: features look back 24 h and outcomes forward 24 h; long-run adoption, retention, maintenance and dependency incorporation are not observed. Bots are identified only by the '[bot]' login suffix; other automation accounts remain in the data. Units are repositories with at least one star or fork on the day (or created that day): the model says nothing about the large majority of repositories with no such activity. Next-day stars for the test day (2024-10-10) come from a Thursday; weekday and holiday patterns are not modelled. The negative-binomial dispersion was fitted on training rows; the simulated distribution's tail (q99.9) should be compared with the report before using the model for viral outliers.",
 "extrapolation_limits": [
  "Population: public GitHub, 2024-10-07..10 UTC (four weekdays of one autumn week). Developers on GitHub are skewed towards professional, English-speaking and North-American/European/Asian time zones; private repositories and private activity are invisible.",
  "GH Archive records the public events API, which drops events under load and omits some activity; counts are lower bounds.",
  "Stars are cheap signals inflated by automation and star farming; a star is not evidence of useful adoption (MASTER_SPEC 6.5). These models describe engagement dynamics, not usefulness.",
  "Observational associations only: nothing was randomized, so the models do not say what promotion, ranking or buying stars would cause.",
  "Short horizon: features look back 24 h and outcomes forward 24 h; long-run adoption, retention, maintenance and dependency incorporation are not observed.",
  "Bots are identified only by the '[bot]' login suffix; other automation accounts remain in the data.",
  "Units are repositories with at least one star or fork on the day (or created that day): the model says nothing about the large majority of repositories with no such activity.",
  "Next-day stars for the test day (2024-10-10) come from a Thursday; weekday and holiday patterns are not modelled.",
  "The negative-binomial dispersion was fitted on training rows; the simulated distribution's tail (q99.9) should be compared with the report before using the model for viral outliers."
 ],
